      "assistant_text": "The **Guarded Write Journal** page describes how the guarded write path handles file modifications and potential rollbacks in the agent runtime.\n\nAccording to [[pages/write-journal]], the key points are:\n\n1. **Prior State Recording**: Before any file is overwritten, the journal records the file\u0027s previous state \u2014 either its prior content (if it existed) or a record that it did not exist.\n\n2. **Rollback Mechanism**: If an agent run fails \u2014 due to exceeding a turn cap, an unrecoverable error, or denied write attempts \u2014 the journal can roll back every recorded write in reverse order. This restores previous content for files that existed and deletes newly created files.\n\n3. **All-or-Nothing Semantics**: The journal provides all-or-nothing write semantics without requiring a database transaction. The journal itself acts as an in-memory transaction log for the duration of a single run.\n\n4. **Query Agent Exception**: The Query agent (like the Grimoire agent you\u0027re currently using) never uses the rollback functionality since it has no write tool at all.",
